$$Y_1(s) = U_1(s)G_1(s)$$

$$Y_2(s) = Y_1(s)G_2(s)$$

Sustituyendo $Y_1(s)$ en la segunda ecuación, obtenemos:

$$Y_2(s) = (U_1(s)G_1(s))G_2(s)$$

$$Y_2(s) = U_1(s)G_1(s)G_2(s)$$

